1918)","inception":1806.5260273972603,"dissolved":1918,"enwiki":"Grand Duchy of Baden","summary":"The Grand Duchy of Baden (German: Großherzogtum Baden) was a German polity on the east bank of the Rhine. It originally existed as a sovereign state from 1806 to 1871 and later as part of the German Empire until 1918.\nThe duchy's 12th-century origins were as a margraviate that eventually split into two, Baden-Durlach and Baden-Baden, before being reunified in 1771. The territory grew and assumed its ducal status after the dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire but suffered a revolution in 1848, whose demands had been formulated in Offenburg the previous year at a meeting now considered the first-ever democratic program in Germany."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q186320","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q1040","value_label":"Karlsruhe","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Karlsruhe"},{"qid":"Q186320","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q131339","value_label":"Alemannic","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Alemannic"},{"qid":"Q186320","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q23540","value_label":"Protestantism","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Protestantism"},{"qid":"Q186320","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q41614","value_label":"constitutional monarchy","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"constitutional monarchy"},{"qid":"Q186320","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q12548","value_label":"Holy Roman Empire","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P155","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Holy Roman Empire"},{"qid":"Q186320","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q637238","value_label":"Electorate of Baden","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1365","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Electorate of Baden"},{"qid":"Q186320","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q151624","v